	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape uses the camera for your Mood Scan: a selfie to read your expression, or a fingertip over the back camera with the flash on to read your pulse. Only the reading is used; no photo or video of your fingertip is kept.</string>
	<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape can use your approximate location to tune soundscapes to your local weather and time of day.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape can use your approximate location to tune soundscapes to your local weather and time of day.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape uses the microphone when you choose to talk with Lucille or record a voice journal entry.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape lets you choose a photo from your library for your profile picture or a journal entry.</string>
	<key>NSPushNotification</key>
	<string>In order to send notifications, Escape will need permission to send push notifications when your mood updates.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Escape turns your speech into text when you talk with Lucille or dictate a journal entry.</string>
	<key>PermissionGroupNotification</key>
